S'what I had to do on mine.  I removed the CDROM front panel, slid the bare
chassis up to the VS bezel from inside and marked the corners.  Drilled and
cut between the holes.  That way, the drive slides in from the front and
stops up against the panel. Otherwise you end up cutting a hole big enough
for the whole drive to slide through, which looks even uglier.  I also
vaguely recall having to drill a locating hole in the plastic tray for a
side screw.


