I recently got a used VT-525 terminal, provided with only the power cord.
Can anyone point me to a user's manual online, or is anyone willing to loan
me such a manual for a short time? I haven't a clue how to setup and operate
this unit so as to take advantage of its advanced features. I wouldn't mind
having access to a programmers manual for the VT-525 either. I will be
willing to pay postage both ways if someone has manual(s) to loan.

I played with the thing and managed to get it into setup via the F3 key (by
pressing the key shortly after power-up), and reset it to factory defaults.
That is as far as I have gotten. It would be VERY nice if I knew how to at
least switch sessions...

I am aware than Boundless currently makes these terminals, but haven't seen
a place on their site to download or order a manual for the terminal.

I am hoping to connect the VT-525 to a KVM switch so I can eliminate a
VT-420 terminal and a computer monitor and keyboard. I have a Deserver 300
that I will connect the terminal serial I/O to that will allow me to control
the consoles of several VAXen and Alpha's.

In case anyone wonders, yes, I run OpenVMS on all of the VAXen and all but
one of the Alpha's. I eagerly await Montgar's forthcoming 7.3 release of the
Hobbyist kit.

Thanks,
