some of you might already know vax6k.openecs.org, a freely accessible VAX 6000
system running the OpenVMS 7.3 operating system. Those of you who tried to use
this system over the last few months noticed that it is unavailable. The reason
is easy to explain: no money. Operating a system like that costs about EUR100
per month. Including the cost for 18.5kWh electricity a day and the internet
connection.
There are about 50 registered users on the vax6k.openecs.org system. To keep
this project alive we encourage all users and feature users to donate an
adequate amount of money to this project. We have powered the system up again,
but if we don't receive sufficient funds until 1st January 2003, we're forced to
shut down the service again for an indefinite long time.
Please visit http://vax6k.openecs.org and convince yourself how valuable this
project is. You will find all details on how donate there. Sponsors are welcome
too.

Best Regards - vax6k team


