Wow! Well, I would recommend considering shopping around for MicroVAX
3100s, say model 98 or so and consign the VAX 6000s to museum piece
status. uVAX 31Ks support SCSI, but not SCSI clustering. So, you'd be
looking at LAVc and MSCP serving. That would DRASTICALLY reduce your
electrical energy expenses right there.

Beyond that, unless you've sworn a blood-oath to keep VAX-only alive in
this way, I'd shop around for used Alpha 2100s, 4100s, used CIPCAs and
other CI gear. Alphas are a LOT cheaper to run.

In either case, RZ28s or better are bigger than RA90s, eat a LOT less
power and put out a LOT less heat.

For what that may be worth...

