that some of them require a loopback connector in the serial port.

> Also there are two devices - COMM DSW41/42 2 CHANNEL V3.11-47 

Synchronous port controllers (see below).

> and ASYNC DHW41/2 V1.6 - What are they?

Async port controllers (see below).
 
> On the back side of box there are 2 ports looks like SCSI ports (like
> small 50 pin centronics, femail, don't remember connector name) called
> "A" and "B" with two arrows.

Either a pair of 8-line data-line-only asynchronous ports (DHW42-BA),
or a pair of 4-line async ports with modem control (DHW42-CA). You may
need to boot the system to find out which you have (SHOW DEVICE TX on
VMS). The -BA uses an H3104 "Harmonica" to provide DEC423 connections
from the centronics connectors. It's a simple passive device (i.e. no
electronic devices) for which wiring information is given at
http://www.vaxarchive.org/hw/cables.html#bc16c . The -CA uses a
BC29J-06 breakout cable to DB-25 connectors, but I don't have a URL
for details on this.

> On the center there are also 2 50 pin DB-?? connectors with 3 rows of
> pins, called "0" and "1" with two arrows, the upper one arrow has
> "impuls" sign.

For synchronous modems. I forget the speed, but quite slow and
probably of little use nowadays.

Chris


