In 1965 ICs were much too expensive for general use.  By 1970
individual transistors were much too expensive for general use,
even though their prices had fallen.  Things have been relatively
stable since then in the glue world, except that 7400 stuff is and
has been replaced by a few FPLA types, once more reducing packages
and interconnects.

After all, you CAN build almost anything out of nothing but 7400
quad 2-NANDs :-)

