Well, I wanted to try hobbesthevax when I got my first VAX.
At that time I only had ULTRIX and I wanted to play with
VMS somewhere to check out if it was worth the work to get
it on a MicroVAX II. So I subscribed to hobbesthevax.
I almost never heard from them. 1.5 months later I got a
VAXstation 3100 and it was easier to install VMS there.
I had almost forgotten about hobbesthevax.
About 2 or 3 months after I subscribed some guy from
hobbesthevax called me at 3am in the morning (Hello?
Germany is not quite on the US side of the globe, right?)
to verify my identity. He wanted to talk with me about
VMS on my MicroVAX II too, but I really wasn't in the
mood to say more than 5 words in one sentence.
Finally he gave me my password and said that it would be
enabled in a few days.
To give this story a sad end, I tried about one month
to log in, but my password was never accepted (and I'm
sure that I wrote it down correctly)
I really like the feature of the guest account at 
vax6k.openecs.org. You can log in and see how VMS looks.
For a permanent account most people will get a VAX on
their own anyway.

