I recently came into possession of a small Digital computer. It's
about 12" x 12" x 2" in size. It has a serial port, parallel port,
network port and mini-50 pin SCSI port in the back.Onboard video too.
Mouse and keyboard ports. There is a (missing) sliding cover in the
front, next to a round power button with a light in it. 2 thumbscrews
in the back allow the mainboard to slide out. There's 4 72 pin RAM
slots and the CPU is covered by a screw-on finned aluminum heatsink.

I can't find any model number stamped anywhere, but the mainboard has
a sticker that says: TA50602113. It powers on but I get no video,
perhaps because I don't have the correct RAM in it. Theres no disk but
one could be plugged into a riser card by unplugging a very short
cable that goes to the ext. SCSI plug (the cable is dated 0195.) I
currently have no ext SCSI disk to check this out.

The tray has what appears to be space for a floppy (3.5"), but a hdd
is too long to fit in the space. Just checked; a floppy drive is too
long too. There's a pci slot in the riser card, and, strangely enough,
two pcmcia slots in the back; type 1 I think (they're thin.)

Anyone know what this is, and how powerful it might be? Is it worth
fixing up to fool around with, say, linux or BSD?


