Well, RZ29B-VA is a narrow-SCSI 4GB disk for use in a BA350 or BA356 (I
think) storage shelf.

BA350 shelves are narrow-SCSI only. BA356 shelves can be either narrow
or wide, but need a "personality module" to be one or the other - they
don't connect directly to the SCSI bus.

I'm familiar with the old Prioris machines, but not a "zx" (that's a
newer, HP-badged box, no?).

