The number one thing which restricts a remote login using X on more recent
systems is usually people neglecting to set xhost.  Many systems deny
access to X from remote by default because of the nasty sorts of attacks
that people can launch from it (with the right savvy).

Could be software misconfiguration on his NT side (I use XWin32 just
fine).  After that, it might be port filtering.

