According to the KDF11B-A User's Guide and posters to this thread, TX
and RX (and GND) are the only RS232 lines offered by the SLU, so the
problem could not have been control signals.

I actually got a fully functioning console when I replaced the null
modem cable I was using, with a factory made modem(?) cable.
Presumably TX and RX were incorrectly swapped (I assumed the SLU port
was DTE, so I originally tried a null modem cable). I haven't had time
to properly confirm this cause yet (my weekend was spent setting up an
AlphaStation with Linux rather than playing with PDP).

