RS232 is pretty tolerant of faults - each pin should be able to tolerate +/-
35 volts wrt signal ground, without damage. However RS423, used on more
recent equipment, has lower voltages, normally +/- 5v. I just wondered
whether a faulty terminal might be sending an excessive voltage on one pin,
breaking through the input protection, and damaging a chip on the controller
board. It is unlikely, but there aren't many things that would stop both of
your controllers from booting.

