For the record, what worked for me was the following 10-pin to DB25
female "adapter" cable (which is then connected to a null modem
cable):

IDC           DB25
 3 (XMIT+) ->  2
 8 (RCV+)  ->  3
 2 (GND)   ->  7 
               8 & 20 jumpered
*** If you want to use a single cable from SLU to DTE/terminal, swap
XMIT and RCV in the pinout above ***  (Some suggest also tying IDC pin
7 RCV- to GND, but this worked without it.)

Because I was using the extra null modem cable, the pinout above is
reversed from that shown in the handwritten notes to Table 13-7, page
13-5, of the KDF11-BA CPU Module User's Guide (
http://www.spies.com/~aek/pdf/dec/pdp11/KDF11BA_UsersManual.pdf ),
also described by respondents to this thread, which has the signals
already swapped as a null modem cable would. So my first attempt was a
classic case of doublethink (halfthink?)

I do it this way, with 2 cables, because then I can use the same null
modem cable on my terminal-emulator to connect to any of my boxes with
serial consoles (SPARC, HP, etc). The adapter cable described above
leaves me with a female DTE DB25, like the others. But I nearly
outsmarted myself :-)

Thanks again for all the responses.

Toby

